+## Retry or fail fast
+
+Walk the chart top to bottom. The POST check comes before the status code, so a 503 or a timeout on a
+keyless POST ends at the warning, not at a retry row.
+
+```dot
+digraph retry_or_fail_fast {
+    "Call failed or timed out" [shape=ellipse];
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" [shape=plaintext];
+    "Health check exits 0?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is it a POST with no Idempotency-Key?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [shape=octagon, style=filled, fillcolor=red, fontcolor=white];
+    "Is it 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Is it 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [shape=diamond];
+    "Retry up to 3 times (same key for a POST)" [shape=box];
+    "Fail fast and report" [shape=doublecircle];
+
+    "Call failed or timed out" -> "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health";
+    "curl -sf https://status.example.invalid/health" -> "Health check exits 0?";
+    "Health check exits 0?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="no, service is down"];
+    "Health check exits 0?" -> "Is it a POST with no Idempotency-Key?" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a POST with no Idempotency-Key?" -> "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it a POST with no Idempotency-Key?" -> "Is it 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" [label="no"];
+    "Never retry a POST without an idempotency key" -> "Fail fast and report";
+    "Is it 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="yes, fix the request"];
+    "Is it 400, 401, 403, 404, 409 or 422?" -> "Is it 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" [label="no"];
+    "Is it 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Retry up to 3 times (same key for a POST)" [label="yes"];
+    "Is it 502, 503, 504 or a timeout?" -> "Fail fast and report" [label="otherwise"];
+}
+```
